  "releaseNotes": "v0.8.0: IErpQuery<T>.CountAsync asks the provider how many records match the query, for example to show import progress, and returns null when the provider cannot count that resource or that combination of filters. It is a default interface member that returns null without a request, so existing IErpQuery implementations compile and run unchanged. Take caps the count; the count is the provider's own number and can differ from the records returned (for example records skipped for a missing identity).",
